00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:55.730
sono ashiwo tomenna
Don't ever stop

00:01:55.730 --> 00:02:00.340
taoreru nowa mada hayaize
It's too soon to fall down

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:01.810
Breakin' through
Breakin' through

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:03.670
uchinukeyo
Pierce through

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.910
yamiwo hurihodoki
Free yourself from darkness

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:10.210
tadoritsuku bashowa hitotsusa
There is only one destination

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:22.920
A Whale's Feather

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:29.800
It's not like you to wake up
on your own on a day off.

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:30.900
Yeah.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:30.940
Road Map
Yeah.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:32.370
Road Map

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:34.940
Are you going somewhere?

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:36.170
Yeah.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.440
With someone?

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:38.770
Yeah.

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:40.010
Who?

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:41.640
Yup!

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.240
Leaving now!

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.190
Sorry, did you wait long?

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.820
Nope. Not at all!

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:07.910
You mean...

00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:09.300
Just the two of us, alone?

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.200
Is that bad?

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.210
Did you have plans with someone else?

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.340
N-no, not especially.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.180
I'm a good driver, you know?

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:21.980
Sorry that it's also for work.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:24.020
We should get away for a bit.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:27.650
Did I really?

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:31.130
Did I look that down?

00:03:31.130 --> 00:03:32.330
What do you mean?

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.570
You said we should get away.

00:03:34.570 --> 00:03:35.500
Yesterday...

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:38.630
Oh, no, that's not what I meant...

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:40.330
Are you, though?

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:55.680
Oh, yes. I'm listening...

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.760
We haven't had the time to actually talk.

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.590
Even if we didn't run into each other yesterday...

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:03.090
I had been thinking about taking you out.

00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.160
I see...

00:04:18.310 --> 00:04:19.800
A Whale's Feather

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:27.220
Could be from a long, long time ago.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:30.150
Could be from a distant yesterday.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.960
Could be about a land unknown.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.430
Could be about a familiar place.

00:04:35.430 --> 00:04:38.260
This is the story of such a time and place.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.600
Dammit, fine.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.170
What about the other one?

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:46.540
Morimoto Kanaru is at a store near the dorms.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.870
She might be meeting up with Sakakiba Takuro...

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:49.170
and Kayano Megumi, who left early this morning.

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:52.110
Ayanagi City General Hospital
and Kayano Megumi, who left early this morning.

00:04:52.110 --> 00:04:55.480
Ayanagi City General Hospital
Who told you they left in the morning?

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:55.550
Ayanagi City General Hospital
Who told you they left in the morning?
From the dormitory manager, Inui.

00:04:55.550 --> 00:04:57.280
Ayanagi City General Hospital
From the dormitory manager, Inui.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.580
Ayanagi City General Hospital
Um... I didn't notice he was
standing right behind me.

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:02.490
Ayanagi City General Hospital
You're too slow.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:02.710
You're too slow.

00:05:05.090 --> 00:05:07.530
It must be tough.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.390
Things like this are also part
of a medical inspector's job?

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:11.830
Yes...

00:05:37.620 --> 00:05:38.820
No way.

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.060
A feather...

00:06:32.110 --> 00:06:33.040
O-ouch!

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:34.910
Nikaido-san?

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:36.540
Are you alright?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:47.160
You scared me.

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.130
I didn't know you were anemic.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:53.030
I just had a head rush.

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:57.400
What's the difference between
anemia and a head rush?

00:06:57.670 --> 00:07:01.510
They both happen due to a
lack of oxygen in your head.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:03.740
But they're completely different from each other.

00:07:03.740 --> 00:07:07.610
A head rush is a case of cerebral anemia,

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:09.580
which happens when you stand up suddenly, or...

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.410
What?

00:07:12.650 --> 00:07:13.850
Sorry.

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:16.020
I just think it's funny...

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:19.180
that a grown woman would fall and hit her head.

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:22.030
You're being judgmental.

00:07:22.030 --> 00:07:24.500
It doesn't matter how old you are.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.560
True.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:27.670
The age thing doesn't apply to everyone.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:28.720
That's right.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:31.470
Wait, what do you mean?

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:33.170
You haven't changed.

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:38.040
Your clumsiness... like forgetting
your camera's memory card.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.280
You!

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:40.850
Ow, ouch...

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:42.110
Are you okay?

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:43.170
Yeah...

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.310
Oh, I've got a bump.

00:07:46.780 --> 00:07:48.550
It's not big, but...

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:51.850
I'm too old to have a bump on my head.

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:55.050
Don't laugh. Geez.

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:01.250
L-let's go buy a memory card.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:34.800
Me?

00:08:34.800 --> 00:08:36.230
You were good at it.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.860
You still draw, right?

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:41.400
Sometimes... when I feel like it.

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:45.540
You want me to draw instead of taking a picture?

00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:47.410
We couldn't find any memory cards.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:49.910
Is that okay for your records?

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:51.510
It's for your work, right?

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:53.180
Right.

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:57.450
Anyway, Eiko-neecha...

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:01.480
Eiko-san, I didn't know you
transferred to Ayanagi Station.

00:09:01.930 --> 00:09:04.020
You didn't hear from Ryo?

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.620
I see...

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.800
Do you think he's changed? Ryo?

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:13.530
I'm not sure.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:16.340
I don't really get him.

00:09:16.340 --> 00:09:20.280
I don't remember whether he
was like that before or not.

00:09:20.640 --> 00:09:22.840
It has been ten years.

00:09:23.650 --> 00:09:28.410
I know the time we lived together
was shorter than our time apart,

00:09:29.320 --> 00:09:33.650
but I don't think it was like this at all.

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:39.490
Good or bad, he's a stereotypical eldest brother.

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:46.540
He always kept a certain distance
between his younger siblings...

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.510
because he saw himself more as a guardian.

00:09:49.510 --> 00:09:52.600
That feeling has gotten even
stronger over the past ten years...

00:09:53.880 --> 00:09:55.850
It's just how he is.

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:58.770
The whole situation with Yuki-chan, too...

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:04.610
Even if it wasn't Ryo's fault...
he still blames himself.

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:07.820
That's why he's...

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:09.990
What do you mean?

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:12.690
What do you mean by Yuki's situation?

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.890
Why would he blame himself?

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:17.600
Well...

00:10:18.900 --> 00:10:20.390
You don't know?

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:21.930
About what?

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:33.050
I'm still not convinced...

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:35.810
How did this happen?

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.310
I'm so sorry.

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:40.850
I haven't been able to help at all.

00:10:41.090 --> 00:10:44.600
I'm not trying to blame you...

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:47.530
It's just... Why does this keep
happening to our family?

00:10:47.770 --> 00:10:49.930
Has anyone else?

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:53.560
My father, too. Ten years ago.

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:10.520
In the accident ten years ago...

00:11:10.520 --> 00:11:15.790
Yuki-chan suffered a fatal injury
and Jun-kun was severely hurt.

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:18.520
Part of his brain got damaged.

00:11:19.160 --> 00:11:24.370
The options were to either give up on
them both, or try to save Jun-kun's life.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:28.040
Ryo had to make the decision by himself.

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:33.600
He signed the consent form to transplant
part of Yuki-chan's brain to Jun-kun.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.280
I'm sorry.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:40.770
I thought you knew...

00:11:43.890 --> 00:11:46.360
Sometimes, I noticed...

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:50.330
Yuki, inside Jun.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:53.590
I thought it was just because they were twins.

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:59.140
I can't hear Ryo-oniichan's voice...

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:10.550
Thank you, as always.

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:12.880
Don't mention it. I'll see you...

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:15.310
Um, sir...

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:20.820
There's still a little hope.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:25.690
Sometimes... It rarely happens, but...

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:30.130
He smiles.

00:12:44.310 --> 00:12:45.750
Is it that surprising?

00:12:46.250 --> 00:12:50.050
I got my license back when
I started diving in college.

00:12:50.050 --> 00:12:51.490
That's so like you.

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:52.860
What?

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.420
It doesn't surprise me.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:56.190
Sorry, I can't hear you.

00:12:56.830 --> 00:12:59.590
It's so like you, Eiko-neechan!

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:04.290
I was happy.

00:13:05.440 --> 00:13:10.930
Even after ten years, you and
Jun-kun remembered me.

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:12.570
How could I...

00:13:12.710 --> 00:13:14.640
forget?

00:13:33.060 --> 00:13:34.050
Look!

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:38.500
A mirage...

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.310
Have you seen it before?

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:43.670
Just once... when I was little.

00:13:43.940 --> 00:13:46.010
It's been a while for me, too.

00:13:46.010 --> 00:13:48.850
Have you heard about the giant clam?

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:53.680
The mirage is actually the energy
exerted as a giant clam exhales... right?

00:13:53.680 --> 00:13:55.690
You sure are one of the locals.

00:13:55.690 --> 00:14:00.290
Many teachers talked about the
mirage's origin to pass time.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:03.630
I mean, really, how big does this clam have to be?

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:06.690
People back then sure had creative minds,

00:14:07.230 --> 00:14:09.130
since they didn't know much.

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:11.060
I don't know about that.

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:16.340
We still don't know much today.

00:14:17.010 --> 00:14:23.850
Maybe there is something there, and
the people back then could see it.

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:25.180
What would be there?

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:29.890
When I just started getting the hang of diving,

00:14:29.890 --> 00:14:32.720
I was diving alone, away from my friends.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:37.420
I probably had hypothermia.

00:14:38.700 --> 00:14:41.470
I couldn't move my body like I wanted to.

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:43.830
My consciousness was fading.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:48.290
I couldn't tell whether I was sinking or floating...

00:14:49.640 --> 00:14:54.010
...At first, I thought it was the light
coming from the surface of the water.

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:57.770
So I started to try as hard as I could...

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:04.150
but soon I realized...

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:11.060
that the light was coming
from the bottom of the sea.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:15.170
Then I lost consciousness completely.

00:15:15.170 --> 00:15:19.300
When I woke up, I was back
on the boat with my friends.

00:15:20.240 --> 00:15:21.930
A hallucination?

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:24.470
That's what I thought, too...

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:29.670
but what I felt could only happen
in reality... I felt it on my skin...

00:15:43.030 --> 00:15:44.650
Feathers?

00:15:45.430 --> 00:15:47.230
Feathers and singing.

00:15:47.230 --> 00:15:48.700
Isn't that?

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:54.000
The song must be the song
the girl told him about.

00:15:55.110 --> 00:16:01.100
The boy desired to get closer to the
song, so he began to row a boat.

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:06.680
This is where the submarine crew disappeared.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.940
So did my friend, ten years ago...

00:16:10.450 --> 00:16:11.420
Sema Koji

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:15.430
There was a feather left on the boat she was on.

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:18.060
I can't find it in any books.

00:16:18.060 --> 00:16:21.190
And it vanishes before you know it.

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:24.290
Back in the submarine earlier, too...

00:16:26.070 --> 00:16:27.830
A Whale's Feather...

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:31.810
I thought of that book, too.

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:33.840
Such a deep story...

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:36.140
You can interpret it in so many ways.

00:16:36.450 --> 00:16:42.750
My mom said the story is supposed to
make all the people you hold dear happy.

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:52.300
While on a journey to save the
corrupted hearts of family and friends,

00:16:52.300 --> 00:16:55.600
a boy meets a girl whose
body is adorned in feathers.

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:58.040
He asked,

00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:03.000
"How can you be so gentle and peaceful?"

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:05.410
The girl answered,

00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:09.010
"I can hear the song."

00:17:09.010 --> 00:17:12.850
"How will I be able to hear the song, too?"

00:17:12.850 --> 00:17:15.480
"Just listen."

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.720
The boy kept searching to hear the song,

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:21.990
and finally noticed the singing...

00:17:23.090 --> 00:17:23.630
It was...

00:17:23.630 --> 00:17:24.460
Lost at Sea
It was...

00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:26.430
Lost at Sea
Coming from the bottom of the sea...

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:33.330
The boy returned home, his
body embraced in feathers.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:37.210
Given the glowing feathers,

00:17:37.210 --> 00:17:40.140
with tears running down their
cheeks, everyone began to cry aloud.

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:44.100
They realized how happy they used to be.

00:17:45.320 --> 00:17:46.870
Eventually...

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:53.890
One by one, the people of the
village left to go... somewhere else.

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:57.330
Everyone that the boy loved...

00:17:57.330 --> 00:18:00.350
...had all gone.

00:18:02.030 --> 00:18:07.800
But the boy's heart was still filled with happiness.

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.240
It's kind of...

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:13.800
far-fetched.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.150
Oops, sorry.

00:18:16.150 --> 00:18:21.140
It's fine... I remember I thought it
was scary the first time I read it.

00:18:22.820 --> 00:18:25.750
I wish I could ask your parents.

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:29.720
What they knew...

00:18:34.560 --> 00:18:36.100
Let's head back.

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:37.570
Oh... sure.

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:41.330
Hey... Why don't you draw
something while we're here?

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:42.660
Here?

00:18:43.110 --> 00:18:44.270
Bad idea, huh?

00:18:44.880 --> 00:18:46.570
I guess it's a little unstable, anyway.

00:18:47.410 --> 00:18:49.410
There's nothing here but water.

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:50.880
You're right...

00:18:55.850 --> 00:18:58.220
Actually, I should draw something.

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:04.350
Me?

00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:12.740
Don't move.

00:19:12.740 --> 00:19:13.900
Sorry.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:24.980
Ryo was saying a while ago...

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:31.590
that he didn't inherit his parents' artistic skills at all.

00:19:31.590 --> 00:19:34.320
Might not seem like it, but he's jealous of you.

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:41.320
You really are good.

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:43.620
You've got your mother's blood.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:46.340
...But this might be too pretty.

00:19:46.340 --> 00:19:48.170
Probably because it got a little shaky.

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:49.500
Hey!

00:19:51.170 --> 00:19:52.110
What's the matter?

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:52.200
omotai kusariwo
The heavy chain

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:58.200
ima hazushite agemashou
I will take it off for you

00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:03.310
jiyuuni naretara
Once you're free

00:22:03.310 --> 00:22:10.080
kokowo habataite yukeruwa
You'll be able to fly away

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:16.820
atashiga samatage
I stood in your way

00:22:16.820 --> 00:22:25.500
ubatte kita madaminu sekai e
and took that world you haven't seen

00:22:25.500 --> 00:22:29.970
tamerau nonara
If you're going to hesitate

00:22:29.970 --> 00:22:38.610
huriharatte ageru sono udewo
I will free that arm for you

00:22:38.610 --> 00:22:43.180
soshite tookue
Then to faraway

00:22:43.180 --> 00:22:49.350
dekirudake tookue
As far away as possible

00:22:49.350 --> 00:22:52.590
aishiteruno
"I love you"

00:22:52.590 --> 00:22:56.290
ikanaideyo
"Don't leave me"

00:22:56.290 --> 00:23:02.890
koware chaukara
I will break

00:23:12.640 --> 00:23:16.210
Diverging destiny is the last hope.

00:23:16.210 --> 00:23:20.480
Ignorance is the final blessing.

00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:25.520
Even so, focusing my eyes and listening,

00:23:25.520 --> 00:23:28.430
embracing the endearing scent.

00:23:28.430 --> 00:23:31.330
Looking for that beloved person.

00:23:31.730 --> 00:23:34.700
A mask I gained by losing my face.

00:23:34.700 --> 00:23:37.670
Sediments of agony that swell and twist.

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:40.700
Separation that cannot be accepted.
